<title>USA: NYSE Unavailables - U.S. Surgical, Catalina Lighting, Rodman &amp; Renshaw Capital and Bernard Chaus.</title>
<headline>NYSE Unavailables - U.S. Surgical, Catalina Lighting, Rodman &amp; Renshaw Capital and Bernard Chaus.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The New York Stock Exchange said on Monday that U.S. Surgical Corp, U.S. Surgical preferred A stock, Catalina Lighting Inc, Rodman &amp; Renshaw Capital Group and Bernard Chaus Inc were not available for after-hours trading because of news.</p>
<p>U.S. Surgical reported fourth-quarter earnings per share of $0.43, up from $0.26 in the same period of 1995. The company also increased its quarterly dividend to $0.04 from $0.02.</p>
<p>The exchange said Corimon SACA, Westmoreland Coal Co and Westmoreland preferred A stock were also unavailable.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
